# port-patches.sh: glm/r8b @ cf4dde927470 over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 4bab856b97f4..1305bda37155); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
lane host: a sliced fill waits for the shared cut another fill is computing (TF_GLM_PREFIX_WAIT, wojo's GLM 0110)

With TF_GLM_FILL=1 prompts that arrive together all fill at once, so eight
requests on one fresh 28k-token system prompt each computed it (prefix_fanout:
31,488 / 85,440 / 199,360 duplicate tokens at 2 / 4 / 8 concurrent). Whole
passes never did: each ends before the next request's lookup.

- lane_host: before a request takes a lane (after spill v2's parking), when an
  admitted fill still has a mark ahead that the request's prompt shares, that
  its own lookup would resume and that adds at least the shared-prefix minimum
  past its memory hit, it waits for the furthest such mark on the prefix list
  (no lane, counted waiting). It goes to the ready list when that fill has
  stood at the mark, its prompt is in, it left (cancelled, failed, requeued)
  or TF_GLM_PREFIX_WAIT_MS passed; its ordinary lookup resumes the cut. A
  request waits only for an admitted fill and only once: no cycle, the oldest
  fill always runs. Only with sliced fills and a prompt cache; never for
  pictures. Counters prefix_waits, prefix_wait_tokens, prefix_wait_timeouts.
- prompt_cache: Store.waitLeast (the recipe's shared_least; 0: no shared cuts,
  no wait) and Store.wouldServe (a state another pass will keep, judged as
  find judges a kept one).
- native/cuda: TF_GLM_PREFIX_WAIT (1 default, 0 off) and TF_GLM_PREFIX_WAIT_MS
  (60000 default, 0 off), read when the core slices fills over a cache; bad
  values fail the start with words.

Tests (core/lane_host_prefix_test.zig, fake sliced backend): 4 requests on one
system prompt compute it once (3 resume at the cut, replies serial), an
unrelated prompt neither waits nor is waited for; a cancelled leader releases
its waiter; a cancelled waiter leaves once; the bound expires; whole passes and
the wait off unchanged; a run under the minimum is not waited for; the setting.
5 of the 8 failed before the host logic.

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo); spill v2's block store design (2,048-token blocks, lineage, the write-at-keep ring, release and fsync order): BadAd84 (https://github.com/BadAd84), MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#118.
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0030-zig-glm-prefix-wait.patch

